-- 36: FRAME READ SET -- a whole Steam MvC2 frame (FUN_140118950 -> FUN_140607d60: sim + render dispatch + walker + submit)
-- emulated in Ghidra p-code on the live dump_live images (runs/20260903-000941, offline match, clock 2239), every ram
-- access logged and attributed; gates: determinism, clock +1, tick writes inside the pre->post diff, tick->dispatcher
-- re-run 50/50 walker fields. Source doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/FRAME-READSET.md (2026-09-03).
-- Apply with tools/re_kb/apply_seed.py (per statement) after the README export backup. Idempotent: UPSERT for nodes,
-- RELATE with explicit edge ids. No apostrophes inside string literals. Do NOT re-run 07_dedup_edges.surql afterwards
-- (it strips confidence/evidence from edges).
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:frame_emulation_20260903 SET kind='ghidra', strength='code', ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/d3dcap/replay/emu_gate.py frame + emu_frame.py + re_map/ghidra_emu/EmuGate.java (trace/functable/image/extstub/callother/heap/extalloc/extret); images d3dcap/ttd/runs/20260903-000941/pre (gitignored)', note='Ghidra 12.1.2 p-code emulation of FUN_140118950 (tick) and FUN_140620960 (dispatcher) on the live images of one process (exe_image 68 MB at 0x140000000, dcram 32 MB at 0xFBC1000, ctx 4 MB at 0xF7C1000, blk 0x33B18 at 0x146C1000, nothing relocated). Every ram access logged (kind, pc, addr, size, ordered), functions by body containment, SH4 pairs from docs/steam_sh4_map.csv. Imports outside the image stubbed (RAX=0, RET) except RtlAllocateHeap/RtlReAllocateHeap = bump allocator and HeapFree/FlsSetValue = 1. Results in docs/FRAME-READSET.md.';

-- routines
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140607d60 SET addr='0x140607d60', name='FUN_140607d60', role='THE FRAME ENTRY of the match scene = *(game_state+0x10): sim (FUN_140608a00) + render table loop (FUN_14060b960 -> FUN_140620960 dispatcher -> FUN_140620f10 walker -> FUN_1406129f0 submit). Called offline by FUN_140039de0 at 0x14003a3ac right after the pad stores 0x14003A33B/0x14003A35F, and by the GGPO wrapper FUN_140118950 via its indirect call.', note='CONFIRMED 2026-09-03 by xrefs (0x14003a3ac COMPUTED_CALL, 0x140118a7a COMPUTED_JUMP, 0x140ac6d50 DATA) and by the whole-frame trace: top-level callees FUN_1408441d0, FUN_140608a00, FUN_14060b960. 459,681 instructions for one idle-ish frame (5 drawn nodes).', matched=false;
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140118950 SET role='GGPO tick wrapper: DAT_142d10b90++, game_state+0x798 = 1, prev=cur shuffle of the four pad words game_state+0x218..0x224 -> +0x228..0x234, pad[seat(k)] = inputs[k] & 0xffffff via the seat map game_state+0x258..0x264, then (*(game_state+0x10))() = FUN_140607d60. The third argument (disconnect flags) is unused.', note='CONFIRMED by decompile + whole-frame emulation 2026-09-03 (docs/FRAME-READSET.md). The pad words are in the game_state struct at 0x140ac6d40 (exe global 0x140AC6F58), NOT in blk.', emu_gate='2026-09-03: emulated on the live images; deterministic (2 runs byte-identical); blk+0x3CC8 2239->2240; 120 blk bytes changed, 116 inside the 237-frame pre->post diff, 4 one-byte anim countdowns outside';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140620960 SET emu_gate_frame='2026-09-03: run again on the state the tick built (LayerZ + G+0x24 reset): 50/50 walker fields identical on 5 drawn nodes, 0 of 211,736 blk bytes differ, quads 125 = 125; deterministic';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14060a1f0 SET addr='0x14060a1f0', name='FUN_14060a1f0', role='PER-FRAME render-list init (NOT init-only): called once per frame by FUN_140609d60 inside FUN_140608a00; FUN_140613390 (LayerZ table reset from DAT_140a6d888 + immediates) executes inside it.', note='CONFIRMED by the whole-frame trace 2026-09-03: the LayerZ writes of FUN_140613390 and the call FUN_140609d60 -> FUN_14060a1f0 are in the tick trace. Resolves finding:emu_gate_layerz_reset_unknown.', matched=false;
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140613390 SET note_frame='2026-09-03: executes every frame (reached by a jump inside FUN_14060a1f0). Besides LayerZ it reads one u32 at +0x48 of 0x38-byte records blk+0x1000 + n*0x38 (128 reads) -- a blk region OUTSIDE the block map (DC UNKNOWN).';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140612430 SET addr='0x140612430', name='FUN_140612430', role='per-fighter sprite-page builder: for each cell of the node sid (via GFX2 +0x1B0 and GFX1 +0x1A8) decodes the part with FUN_140614210 into DC 0x0CE60000 (ctx[1]+0xE60000) and uploads via FUN_1408456a0; sets node+0x120 from blk+0x32BF0; texture-slot bases blk+0x32BE8/+0x32BF0; writes 500 B scratch at 0x142eed950 read by the submit FUN_1406129f0 in the same frame', note='CONFIRMED decompile 2026-09-03 (docs/FRAME-READSET.md s3.2, s3.5); 5 calls per frame on this state; the 0x0CE60000 table (11,488 B) is REBUILT EVERY FRAME, so a snapshot copy of it is torn against blk.', matched=false;
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140614210 SET addr='0x140614210', name='FUN_140614210', role='LZSS part decoder (src, destLen, dest): the only writer of DC RAM in a frame (0x0CE60000..0x0CE62CDF, 11,488 B; 58 calls, 17,039 distinct dcram bytes read from the PL images)', note='CONFIRMED by trace 2026-09-03. SH4 pair INFERRED: loc_8c0354c0 (the plain byte-stream LZSS of seed 21) -- same call shape (part+4, destLen, running dest at 0x0CE60000).', matched=false;
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_1408456a0 SET addr='0x1408456a0', name='FUN_1408456a0', role='texture page upload into the host staging buffer *(game_state+0x208) + *(game_state+0x214) after checking the slot record ctx+0x1e00a0 + TCW*0x18 (format nibble 0x100/0x500/0x700/0x900)', note='CONFIRMED decompile 2026-09-03. Caller FUN_140612430 (125 calls/frame). In the live process the staging buffer sits right after the DC-RAM image (0x11BC1000 = dcram + 32 MB); the frame writes it (64,000 B memset by FUN_140800620 + 750 dwords) and never reads it back.', matched=false;
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_140607e90 SET note_frame='2026-09-03 trace: reads 23 blk bytes and writes game_state+0x4F4, +0x520, +0x5DC..0x5EC (19 B) every frame -- the battle-globals save-slot sync is a DERIVED copy of blk, not independent state.';
UPSERT steam_routine:FUN_14003a4c0 SET note_frame='2026-09-03: the sprintf wrapper (FUN_14003a4b0 + __stdio_common_vsprintf) is called twice per frame from FUN_140627c50 <- FUN_140628320 <- caseD_7. It is the only reason the frame needs the UCRT per-thread data: with imports stubbed to 0 the CRT recursed forever (_calloc_base -> __doserrno -> __acrt_getptd_noexit -> _calloc_base).';

-- globals
UPSERT global:game_state_pad_words SET addr='0x140AC6F58', steam_off='game_state+0x218', type='u32[4]', note='THE per-frame INPUT of the frame: pad word per seat (24-bit), game_state+0x218/+0x21C/+0x220/+0x224; previous frame at +0x228..; seat map game_state+0x258..0x264 (player k -> seat, 0 offline). Written offline by FUN_140039de0 (0x14003A33B/35F) and online by FUN_140118950 from the GGPO-synchronised inputs; translated into blk+0x3C66 by FUN_140048630. Exe global, not blk. CONFIRMED (decompile + trace 2026-09-03).';
UPSERT global:texture_staging_buffer SET addr='*(game_state+0x208)', steam_off='game_state+0x208', type='ptr', note='host texture-staging buffer (pointer at game_state+0x208, cursor at +0x214, cursor2 +0x210): FUN_1408456a0 copies decoded pages here; live it lies right after the DC-RAM image (dcram + 0x2000000). Write-only within a frame (64,755 accesses, 0 reads back). Render output, not state. CONFIRMED site / INFERRED purpose (2026-09-03).';
UPSERT global:tile_table_0CE60000 SET addr='0x0CE60000', steam_off='ctx[1]+0xE60000', type='bytes[0x2CE0]', note='per-frame decoded-part / tile table rebuilt by FUN_140612430 -> FUN_140614210 from the PL images and the node state (11,488 B written, 11,968 B read by the copy FUN_140800620 and 343 B by the submit FUN_1406129f0). Same region as buffer:ce60000 (Texture_Decompress_Buffer). A snapshot copy is torn against blk (2,340 B differ on runs/20260903-000941), which is why the dispatcher alone on a raw dump misses 3 depth fields while tick->dispatcher matches 50/50. CONFIRMED by trace 2026-09-03.';
UPSERT global:blk_unmapped_1000 SET addr='DC UNKNOWN', steam_off='0x1000..0x3C66', type='rec[0x38][~126]', note='blk region between the matrix push storage (0..0x1000) and the input array (0x3C66) is outside the block map; FUN_140613390 reads u32 +0x48 of each 0x38-byte record blk+0x1000+n*0x38 every frame (128 reads) and FUN_14060bab0 reads blk+0x3C40. INFERRED: the per-frame render-list record array. DC counterpart UNKNOWN (2026-09-03).';
UPSERT global:exe_counters_142edf318 SET addr='0x142edf318', steam_off='DAT_142edf318/31C/538/543/546', type='u16,u16,u16,u8,u8', note='five small exe-resident counters read and written inside the frame (FUN_1406163e0 among the writers); role UNKNOWN; the only mutable exe state outside game_state / render bookkeeping that the frame carries across frames (8 B). Include the 0x142edf300 page in a snapshot (2026-09-03).';
UPSERT global:crt_import_slots SET addr='0x1408db240', steam_off='0x1408db240 / 0x1408db140 / 0x1408db238 / 0x1408db218', type='ptr[4]', note='UCRT import slots RtlAllocateHeap / RtlReAllocateHeap / HeapFree / FlsSetValue (call [rip+slot] sites in _calloc_base 0x14081fd19, _realloc_base 0x14082292d, _free_base 0x14081d1a2, __acrt_FlsSetValue 0x140820c2a). emu_frame reads the live targets from these slots so the emulator stubs are boot-independent. CONFIRMED by capstone on the live image 2026-09-03.';

-- findings
UPSERT finding:frame_emulation_deterministic SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='A whole Steam MvC2 frame -- FUN_140118950 -> FUN_140607d60 (sim + render dispatch + sprite walker + submit), 459,681 instructions -- runs to completion in Ghidra p-code on the live dump_live images and is DETERMINISTIC: two runs give byte-identical access streams (313,754 records) and byte-identical blk / game_state / ctx / GGPO / staging dumps. The dispatcher alone (149,903 instr.) likewise. Nothing failed to run: 6 imports (GetLastError, FlsGetValue, RtlAllocateHeap, FlsSetValue, HeapFree, SetLastError) needed by the sprintf path were stubbed (allocator = bump arena), 0 unimplemented instructions.';
UPSERT finding:frame_tick_gate SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='The emulated tick advances blk+0x3CC8 by exactly 1 (2239 -> 2240) and changes 120 blk bytes; 116 of them lie inside the pre->post diff of the live dumps (post = 237 frames later, 7,785 B differ) and the 4 outside are one-byte animation countdowns (fighter[0]+0x186, +0x2FD, +0x398, node+0x186) that had cycled back to the same value. The blk WRITE set of a frame: 6,692 B in 368 ranges (input array, G+0x10..0x27/0x80/0x8A/0x90..0x93/0x98, 55 fighter field runs, 32 node field runs, camera/stage 0x6909..0x6D47 incl. LayerZ, pool bookkeeping, draw lists/counts, battle state 0x32500..0x33B0F).';
UPSERT finding:frame_chain_walker_gate SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='Running FUN_140620960 a second time on the state the tick just built (after resetting LayerZ and G+0x24 exactly as the per-frame init does) reproduces every walker field of every drawn node bit-exact: 50/50 (sx, sy, depth, scx, scy, angle, +0x150, facing, hotx, hoty on 5 nodes), 0 of 211,736 blk bytes differ, quad total 125 = 125, LayerZ 16/16. On the RAW snapshot the dispatcher gets 45/50 (5 depth misses = one extra frame of LayerZ accumulation) and 47/50 with LayerZ reset (3 depth misses = quad-count deltas from the torn 0x0CE60000 tile table). So the render pass is a pure, deterministic function of blk + the frame-built tile table + ctx slot table + exe constants.';
UPSERT finding:frame_entry_is_whole_frame SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='FUN_140607d60 = *(game_state+0x10) is the match-scene frame entry and contains BOTH the simulation (FUN_140608a00) and the render table loop (FUN_14060b960 -> FUN_140620960 -> FUN_140620f10 -> FUN_1406129f0). Offline it is called by FUN_140039de0 at 0x14003a3ac right after the pad stores; online FUN_140118950 wraps it (counter++, game_state+0x798 = 1, pad shuffle, seat-mapped pad writes, indirect call). The pad words live at game_state+0x218..0x224 (0x140AC6F58) in the exe, not in blk. The per-frame LayerZ reset is FUN_14060a1f0 (called each frame by FUN_140609d60) via FUN_140613390.';
UPSERT finding:frame_readset SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='Per-frame READ SET (runs/20260903-000941, 5 drawn nodes): blk 10,004 B in 887 ranges -- input array 40 B, G 52 B, 100 fighter field runs, 39 node field runs, camera/stage 186 B, pool bookkeeping, draw lists/counts, battle state, and blk+0x1000..0x3C66 (outside the block map); dcram 22,545 B in 227 ranges -- PL slot 0 (0x0C42006C..0x0C55D7E8) 4,101 B, PL slot 1 (0x0C810200..0x0C94D7E8) 5,884 B, the frame-built 0x0CE60000 table 11,968 B, effects bank 28 B, HUD bank 544 B, stage POL 20 B; exe 2,445 B -- 400 constant addresses (LayerZ table, sin/cos, input bit table, tile layout tables, game_state read-only fields) + 478 read-and-written (pad words, staging cursor, render-table bookkeeping DAT_142ec4370.., 0x142eed950 scratch, DAT_142ef0ab8, DAT_142d10b90, 0x142edf318..546); ctx 1,871 B -- texture slot table ctx+0x1e0030..0x1e31CA and matrix state ctx+0x1f80a4..0x1f8564. WRITE SET: blk 6,692 B, dcram 11,488 B (0x0CE60000), exe 716 B, ctx 43,217 B (TA records ctx+0x30.., +0x30030.., texture pages +0x100030..0x108FC0), staging buffer 64 KB. The dispatcher alone reads blk 7,265 B / dcram 1,384 B / exe 1,144 B / ctx 933 B and writes exactly the TAPE-V3-SPEC s10.1 fields.';
UPSERT finding:frame_minimum_tape SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', contribution_candidate=true, note='MINIMUM TAPE, derived from the read set: ONE blk snapshot (211,736 B; plus the game_state page 0x140ac6d40+0x1000, the 0x142edf300 page and the ctx texture-slot table, ~1.3 KB) and the TWO seat words per frame (game_state+0x218/+0x21C = tape column seat_in[2]) let the emulated FUN_140118950 regenerate every render input -- node fields, LayerZ, the 0x0CE60000 tile table, the TA records and texture pages in ctx -- byte-exact and deterministically. Per-frame blk diffs are redundant (the tick output IS the diff). Everything else comes from outside the tape and is static per roster/stage: the exe image, the arc-derived DC-RAM data (effects/HUD/stage banks by AFS entry, loaders CONFIRMED in seed 31; the six per-character PL images at 0x0C420000 + k*0x150000 in slot order 0,2,4,1,3,5 -- loader table UNKNOWN, dump-once per roster is the workaround), the bank-loader-built ctx slot table. Every state column of TAPE-V3-SPEC s10 / GS_SCHEMA 0.3.39 is a WRITE of the frame, hence derivable; only seat_in and frame are inputs. OPEN before a pixel-perfect offline frame: the PL loader table, the 8 UNKNOWN exe bytes, and gating on an effect-heavy frame and a second roster (this gate covers one idle-ish frame of one roster).';
UPSERT finding:frame_capgate_roster_mismatch SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', note='Gate (iv) -- tick(frame N) vs capgate frame N+1 -- is NOT RUNNABLE on the available data: the capgate consecutive walk runs (4329..4508, 7279..7458) have roster 0x134/0x2A/0x12A/0x34/0x12C/0x2C while the dcram images have 0x12A/0x34/0x12C/0x117/0x134/0x135 (runs 000941/000956/001249/001259) or 0x12C/0x117/0x134/0x10F/0x12A/0x34 (001536). First divergence: slot 0 +0x6C0 = 0x134 vs 0x12A; every host pointer in the fighter structs (+0x1C0 = 0x12531000.. vs 0x10111000..) differs. A same-roster dump_live session is required.';
UPSERT finding:frame_ucrt_recursion_trap SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-03', note='With every import stubbed to return 0, the first tick emulation never returned: the sprintf wrapper FUN_14003a4c0 needs UCRT per-thread data; __acrt_getptd_noexit -> FlsGetValue (0) -> _calloc_base -> RtlAllocateHeap (0) -> __doserrno -> __acrt_getptd_noexit -> ... (60 M instructions, 1.64 M external calls). Fix: RtlAllocateHeap/RtlReAllocateHeap = bump allocator (size in R8/R9), HeapFree/FlsSetValue = 1, targets read from the live IAT slots. The synthesised stack must also avoid the images: the first smoke run placed it at 0x10000000 INSIDE the dcram image (0xFBC1000..0x11BC1000) -- emu_frame asserts the hole now.';
UPSERT finding:emu_gate_layerz_reset_unknown SET status='superseded', superseded_by='finding:frame_entry_is_whole_frame', note_resolution='2026-09-03: the per-frame resetter is FUN_14060a1f0 (called each frame by FUN_140609d60); FUN_140613390 executes inside it every frame (whole-frame trace).';

